Follow the operating laws in `AGENTS.md` at the repository root. Read it before planning or
editing. It is the single source of truth for engineering policy in this repository.

Do not restate or duplicate its content here.

`AGENTS.md` contains an "External law loading" table. When the task in front of you matches a
row, read that law file before implementing. Do not preload all laws.

Non-negotiable, restated here only because they are irreversible:

- Never mutate git state (add, commit, push, reset, stash, rebase, merge) without an explicit
  per-operation imperative from the user. Questions are not authorization.
- Never claim validation from a test that short-circuits before the new code path.
